{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"M0|recorded corpus|recorded-corpus|chatty|tool-heavy|parallel-tool|aborted-turn|error-result\\\" docs packages src test --glob '\"'!packages/pi-lhc/dist/**'\"' --glob '\"'!node_modules/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"rg: src: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: test: No such file or directory (os error 2)\npackages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:32:/** A loaded corpus: synthetic PI source messages (the stand-in until M0\npackages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:266:/** Replay a recorded corpus through the converter into the temp thread, then\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/test-plan.md:18:Fixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/epic.md:63:- Epic 03's Story 0 fixture (deterministic provider, ~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle, manufactured failure states) is reusable here and extends with mutation-in-flight states; no new fixture family.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/epic.md:81:- **TC-1.1** (AC-1.1, AC-1.3): Overview shape variants: fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls. The compacted tool-heavy fixture asserts exact expected counts (messages by kind, turns, chunks, derivation states, view summary, boundary).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/epic.md:143:The sequence (PI-extension call order): create thread → intake multi-turn tool-heavy batches → background drain settles → status → compact (profile) → pull → inspect (overview, view, health) → edit + delete → rebuild drains → health confirms → second compact → pull → materialize.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:27:- **TC-1.1** (AC-1.1, AC-1.3): Overview shape variants: fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls. The compacted tool-heavy fixture asserts exact expected counts (messages by kind, turns, chunks, derivation states, view summary, boundary).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md:13:**Scope In:** Scripted sequence: create thread → intake multi-turn tool-heavy batches → background drain settles → status → compact (profile) → pull → inspect (overview, view, health) → edit + delete → rebuild drains → health confirms → second compact → pull → materialize.\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:2:// named lifecycle paired with the LHC intake events it should produce. Until M0\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:23:    name: \"chatty\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:44:    name: \"tool-heavy\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:71:    name: \"parallel-tool\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:99:    name: \"error-result\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:120:    name: \"aborted-turn\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:138:  chatty: loadChattyCorpus,\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:139:  \"tool-heavy\": loadToolHeavyCorpus,\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:140:  \"parallel-tool\": loadParallelToolCorpus,\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:141:  \"error-result\": loadErrorResultCorpus,\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:142:  \"aborted-turn\": loadAbortedTurnCorpus,\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:18:- The derived-thread fixture: a recorded conversation (~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle) drained through real Epic 02 machinery into known form states — ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked — plus a canonical-corruption variant (Epic 01 fixture pattern) and a turnless-straggler variant (selection rule 6 / golden G4)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:86:The fixture conversation shape is pinned in the design (~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle): the tool-heavy middle is what gives Story 4 a realistic over-max zone, and the 4 chunks give Story 2's coverage edge something to exclude. Scripted provider failures manufacture the failed states (retryable-fail-exhaust for transient; non-retryable for permanent); blocked comes from source damage on a sacrificial sibling fixture, not the main one. FC-0.4 is the Story 3 gate's fixture-side proof — if it can't pass because Epic 02's persisted reason is opaque, stop and surface it immediately; that's the named Epic 02 patch trigger, not something to work around.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:370:The Story-0 fixture is the load-bearing test asset: one recorded conversation (~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle) drained through real Epic 02 machinery into known form states — ready everywhere, plus manufactured failed-transient (provider fake scripted retryable-fail-exhaust on named subjects), failed-permanent (scripted non-retryable), blocked (source damage via the Epic 01 corruption pattern on a sacrificial sibling fixture), and a canonical-corruption variant. States reached through production paths, never hand-written rows; fixture invariant tests prove each state by read-back before any story consumes it.\npackages/lhc/test/inspect-view.test.ts:117:// The TC-2.1 substrate: the tool-heavy fixture with one degraded entry and\npackages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts:2:// WITHOUT serving anything to a model: each recorded corpus replays through the\npackages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts:98:    // tool-heavy carries tool_call/tool_result correlation ids, so this also\npackages/pi-lhc/test/v